#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Soften DS3's fog and haze particles by widening their depth fade.

    tools/ds3-fog-soften                     # build the m32 (Archdragon Peak) override
    tools/ds3-fog-soften --dry-run           # list what would change, write nothing
    tools/ds3-fog-soften --binder commoneffects --dry-run
    tools/ds3-fog-soften --fade-fraction 0.35 --fade-max 20

WHAT IT DOES AND WHY
--------------------
Donnie on Archdragon Peak: "the way it clips through everything so it does not
feel like it is coming from the doors or in the room, like it is placed on top
of the screen." That is a soft-particle failure, and it is measurable.

Every fog wisp and haze sheet is a camera-facing quad. DS3 does have soft
particles: 376 of the 456 BillboardEx actions in the m32 binder already have
`depthBlend = true`. But the fade band is left at its default everywhere.
Across the 569 appearance actions in m32 that carry the depth fields,
`unkDepthBlend1` is:

    1.0 x507   2.0 x26   2.5 x14   0.5 x11   1.5 x6   0.1 x3   0.25 x1   0.75 x1

and `unkDepthBlend2` is 0.0 on 566 of 569. A default fade band on a sprite
scaled to 30 m or 100 m is nothing, so the quad reaches the floor at full
opacity and you see the intersection line. The fix is to make the band a
function of the sprite instead of a constant: 25 percent of the particle width
by default, clamped to 2..15, so a 7 m wisp gets 2.0 and a 100 m haze sheet
gets 15.0. Whether those numbers are metres or a multiplier on the default is
NOT known, see the field section below, but both readings widen the band.

WHICH PARTICLES
---------------
Only big fog and smoke sprites. The selection is texture id plus size:

  * texture in FOG_TEXTURES (the 8x8 flipbook smoke sheets s11630, s11633,
    s11617, s11624, s11626, s11621, s11623 and the radial haze blobs s50065,
    s50255), and
  * width (max over the keyframes, since 389 of 508 widths are curves) >= 5 m.

Textures 3000 and 1001 are glows and are deliberately NOT in the set: a glow
that fades near geometry loses the bloom that is the whole point of it.

WHY BYTE PATCHING, NOT RE-SERIALISING
-------------------------------------
@cccode/fxr reads and writes DS3 FXRs, but read -> write is not byte-faithful.
Measured on all 136 m32 files: every file returns at the SAME LENGTH and every
file differs in content, from 8 bytes (f000432002) to 17,555 bytes
(f000221504, 16 percent of the file). The differences are structural rather
than semantic (a trailing 0x01 marker the library writes as 0x00, a 255 count
written back as 256, section offsets moved by 16, zeroed offset slots filled
in). We are shipping vanilla map files as a game override, so we do not want
17k bytes of churn per file for a two-dword edit. The node half of this tool
therefore uses the library only to READ, then locates each action's
fields1+fields2 block in the original bytes by exact match and overwrites the
two dwords. Byte-identical to vanilla apart from the intended floats, and the
tool proves it: it diffs the patched buffer against the original and refuses to
write any file with a byte changed outside the dwords it named.

WHAT THE DEPTH FIELDS ACTUALLY ARE (researched 3 Sep 2026, be honest about it)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
`depthBlend` (fields1 index 14) is documented and unambiguous: the soft-particle
toggle. "If enabled, they will instead display in front of the object if they
are close enough, and will fade out with distance from the object's surface
that is blocking the view of the particle."

`unkDepthBlend1` and `unkDepthBlend2` are DS3 fields2 indices 22 and 23, which
land on on-disk dwords 25 and 26 because bloomColor is a Vector4 that eats four
slots. Both are literally "Unknown float." in @cccode/fxr, and the public
record has nothing better:

  * RainbowStoneFXR (ividyon) and the community ER FXR Notes sheet, which share
    a source, both say only "These two fields control how the depth blending
    effect works, but exactly how is unknown."
  * The older DS3 FXR Notes sheet is the most useful line anyone has written:
    field 25 "Always >0. Some scale or something, maybe?", field 26 "Always 0".
  * Zero issues, discussions or commits in EvenTorset/fxr about either field,
    and no one anywhere has published a before/after test.

Two traps worth writing down. First, @cccode/fxr tags unkDepthBlend2 with
ScaleCondition.Distance, which looks like a claim that it is a world distance in
metres. It is not: that flag arrived in a bulk sweep (abae51f, "Scaling is now
data driven", 329 flags in one commit) and was reclassified in a second bulk
sweep (55d42f2). When the same author DID identify a neighbouring field he said
so in the changelog ("unk_ds3_f2_29 has been identified as some kind of view
distance threshold"). No such claim exists for unkDepthBlend2. Second, the
advice floating around to zero unk_sdt_f2_32 before testing depth blending does
not apply here: that field only exists from Sekiro onward, DS3's fields2 list
stops at unk_ds3_f2_29.

So the honest reading of the vanilla numbers is that unkDepthBlend1 is a
unitless SCALE on the depth falloff rather than a distance in metres: it is 1.0
by default, it is the only one of the pair authors ever varied, and its whole
range across the map is 0.1 to 2.5. unkDepthBlend2 is 0 in 566 of 569 instances
(the three exceptions, 100/500/1000, are all in f000832002), which rules it out
as THE fade distance since depth blending demonstrably works with it at zero.

That is why this tool defaults to --field unkDepthBlend1. Under either reading
raising it widens the fade band, which is the direction we want. But note that
the default clamp tops out at 15.0, which is six times the largest value
FromSoft ever authored, so if the field is a multiplier the biggest haze sheets
may fade too eagerly near geometry. Judge it on the TV and pull --fade-max
down to 4 or 5 if the haze reads as thin. The definitive test is a live sweep
with fxr-reloader (EvenTorset/fxr-reloader hot-reloads FXRs into a running
game): 0 / 0.1 / 1 / 10 / 100 on one wall-intersecting particle would settle
what nobody has published.

The binder itself is repacked with soulstruct (same entry ids, paths, flags and
sizes) and recompressed with oodle.dcx_compress_dflt. Note that soulstruct's
BND4 writer appends ten zero pad bytes after every entry's data block "for
byte-perfect writes", which for this binder (whose entries are already
16-aligned and packed tight) means the rebuilt container is 1352 bytes larger
than vanilla: 135 gaps of 10 bytes, less an 8-byte shift of the data region.
The recorded entry sizes and offsets are correct, so this is padding only.

Nothing is written into the game install or the mod folder. The build lands in
data/ds3-ui-port/build/fog/ and the tool prints the copy command.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
from pathlib import Path

HOME = Path.home()
COUCH = HOME / "couch"
UI_PORT = COUCH / "data/ds3-ui-port"
VENV_PY = UI_PORT / ".venv/bin/python"
FXR_NODE = UI_PORT / "fxr-node"
SOULS_EXTRACT = COUCH / "tools/souls-extract"
GAME = HOME / ".steam/steam/steamapps/common/DARK SOULS III/Game"
KEYS_CS = UI_PORT / "uxm_keys.cs"
SFX_CACHE = UI_PORT / "extract/ds3/sfx"
BUILD = UI_PORT / "build/fog"

BINDERS = {
    "m32": "/sfx/frpg_sfxbnd_m32_effect.ffxbnd.dcx",
    "commoneffects": "/sfx/frpg_sfxbnd_commoneffects_effect.ffxbnd.dcx",
}

# The fog and smoke sprite ids, read out of the m32 billboards. 11630/11633 and
# friends are the 8x8 flipbook smoke sheets (128 px a frame); 50065 and 50255
# are the small radial haze blobs used for the ambient sheets at 30 m and 100 m.
FOG_TEXTURES = [11630, 11633, 11617, 11624, 11626, 11621, 11623, 50065, 50255]

# soulstruct only lives in the ds3-ui-port venv; re-exec into it rather than
# making the caller remember which python to use.
if "soulstruct" not in sys.modules:
    try:
        import soulstruct  # noqa: F401
    except ModuleNotFoundError:
        if VENV_PY.exists() and os.environ.get("_DS3_FOG_REEXEC") != "1":
            os.environ["_DS3_FOG_REEXEC"] = "1"
            os.execv(str(VENV_PY), [str(VENV_PY), __file__, *sys.argv[1:]])
        raise

sys.path.insert(0, str(SOULS_EXTRACT))
import oodle  # noqa: E402
from soulstruct.containers import Binder  # noqa: E402


def ds3_keys() -> dict[str, str]:
    txt = KEYS_CS.read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig")
    m = re.search(
        r"DarkSouls3Keys\s*=\s*new Dictionary<string, string>\s*\{(.*?)\n\s*\};",
        txt, re.S)
    return dict(re.findall(
        r'\["([^"]+)"\]\s*=\s*@"(-----BEGIN RSA PUBLIC KEY-----.*?-----END RSA PUBLIC KEY-----)"',
        m.group(1), re.S))


def fetch_binder(name: str) -> Path:
    """Return the vanilla .ffxbnd.dcx, pulling it out of the archives once.

    Read-only on the game install: DvdBnd mmaps the .bdt files and never writes.
    """
    archive_path = BINDERS[name]
    dst = SFX_CACHE / Path(archive_path).name
    if dst.exists():
        return dst
    sys.path.insert(0, str(SOULS_EXTRACT))
    from dvdbnd import DvdBnd, DS3
    SFX_CACHE.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    data = DvdBnd(GAME, ds3_keys(), DS3).get(archive_path)
    if data is None:
        raise SystemExit(f"{archive_path} not found in the DS3 archives")
    dst.write_bytes(data)
    return dst


def run_node(cfg: dict) -> dict:
    work = Path(cfg["report"]).parent
    cfg_path = work / "fog_cfg.json"
    cfg_path.write_text(json.dumps(cfg))
    subprocess.run(
        ["node", "fog_soften.mjs", str(cfg_path)],
        cwd=FXR_NODE, check=True)
    return json.loads(Path(cfg["report"]).read_text())


def fmt_table(changes: list[dict], field: str) -> str:
    if not changes:
        return "  (nothing matched)"
    head = f"  {'effect':<12} {'action':<24} {'fog tex':<12} {'width':>8} {'old':>7} {'new':>7}"
    lines = [head, "  " + "-" * (len(head) - 2)]
    for c in sorted(changes, key=lambda c: (c["file"], -(c["width"] or 0))):
        lines.append(
            f"  {c['file']:<12} {c['action']:<24} {c['fogTextures']:<12} "
            f"{(c['width'] or 0):>8.2f} {c['oldFade']:>7.2f} {c['newFade']:>7.2f}"
            + ("" if c["oldDepthBlend"] else "   [depthBlend off -> on]"))
    return "\n".join(lines)


def main() -> None:
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])
    ap.add_argument("--binder", choices=sorted(BINDERS), default="m32")
    ap.add_argument("--min-width", type=float, default=5.0,
                    help="metres; only particles at least this wide are touched")
    ap.add_argument("--fade-fraction", type=float, default=0.25,
                    help="depth fade band as a fraction of the particle width")
    ap.add_argument("--fade-min", type=float, default=2.0, help="metres")
    ap.add_argument("--fade-max", type=float, default=15.0, help="metres")
    ap.add_argument("--field", default="unkDepthBlend1",
                    choices=["unkDepthBlend1", "unkDepthBlend2"])
    ap.add_argument("--textures", default=",".join(str(t) for t in FOG_TEXTURES),
                    help="comma-separated texture ids to treat as fog")
    ap.add_argument("--no-force-depth-blend", action="store_true",
                    help="leave depthBlend alone instead of turning it on")
    ap.add_argument("--use-height", action="store_true",
                    help="size a particle by max(width, height) instead of width")
    ap.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true",
                    help="report only, write no FXRs and no binder")
    ap.add_argument("--roundtrip-check", action="store_true",
                    help="also measure what a full library re-serialise would cost")
    ap.add_argument("--out", type=Path, default=None)
    args = ap.parse_args()

    src = fetch_binder(args.binder)
    payload = oodle.dcx_decompress(src.read_bytes())
    binder = Binder.from_bytes(payload)
    print(f"{src.name}: {len(payload)} bytes payload, {len(binder.entries)} entries")

    work = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="ds3-fog-"))
    (work / "in").mkdir()
    (work / "out").mkdir()
    by_name = {}
    for entry in binder.entries:
        name = entry.path.replace("\\", "/").rsplit("/", 1)[-1]
        by_name[name] = entry
        (work / "in" / name).write_bytes(entry.data)

    cfg = {
        "dir": str(work / "in"),
        "out": str(work / "out"),
        "report": str(work / "report.json"),
        "textures": [int(t) for t in args.textures.split(",") if t.strip()],
        "minWidth": args.min_width,
        "fadeFraction": args.fade_fraction,
        "fadeMin": args.fade_min,
        "fadeMax": args.fade_max,
        "field": args.field,
        "forceDepthBlend": not args.no_force_depth_blend,
        "useHeight": args.use_height,
        "dryRun": args.dry_run,
        "roundtripCheck": args.roundtrip_check,
    }
    report = run_node(cfg)

    if report["unparsed"]:
        print("\nfiles that did not parse (passed through untouched):")
        for u in report["unparsed"]:
            print(f"  {u['file']}: {u['error']}")
    else:
        print("all entries parsed")

    if report.get("roundtrip"):
        rt = report["roundtrip"]
        print(f"\nlibrary re-serialise round trip: {rt['byteIdentical']}/{rt['total']} "
              f"byte-identical; worst churn "
              + ", ".join(f"{w['file']} {w['nDiff']}B" for w in rt["worst"]))

    changed_files = [f for f in report["files"] if f["patched"]]
    stray = sum(f["strayBytes"] for f in changed_files)
    print(f"\n{len(report['changes'])} particles in {len(changed_files)} effects matched "
          f"(fade = {args.fade_fraction:g} x width, clamped {args.fade_min:g}..{args.fade_max:g})")
    print(fmt_table(report["changes"], args.field))
    if report["skipped"]:
        print("\nskipped:")
        for s in report["skipped"]:
            print(f"  {s}")
    print(f"\nbyte proof: {sum(f['bytesChanged'] for f in changed_files)} bytes changed "
          f"across {len(changed_files)} files, {stray} of them outside the named dwords "
          f"({'OK' if stray == 0 else 'FAIL'}); "
          f"all {len(changed_files)} patched files re-parse: "
          f"{all(f['reparses'] for f in changed_files)}")

    if args.dry_run:
        print("\ndry run, nothing written")
        shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)
        return
    if stray:
        raise SystemExit("refusing to build: stray byte changes")
    if not changed_files:
        print("\nnothing to build")
        shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)
        return

    for f in changed_files:
        by_name[f["file"]].data = (work / "out" / f["file"]).read_bytes()
    rebuilt = binder.to_bytes()
    out = args.out or (BUILD / src.name)
    out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    out.write_bytes(oodle.dcx_compress_dflt(rebuilt))

    # Prove the shipped file loads: decompress it again, reopen the container,
    # and read the edited FXRs back out of it with the library.
    back = oodle.dcx_decompress(out.read_bytes())
    b2 = Binder.from_bytes(back)
    same_ids = [e.entry_id for e in binder.entries] == [e.entry_id for e in b2.entries]
    same_paths = [e.path for e in binder.entries] == [e.path for e in b2.entries]
    same_flags = [e.flags for e in binder.entries] == [e.flags for e in b2.entries]
    print(f"\nbuilt {out} ({out.stat().st_size} bytes dcx, {len(rebuilt)} payload, "
          f"vanilla payload {len(payload)}, +{len(rebuilt) - len(payload)} soulstruct pad)")
    print(f"  reopens: {len(b2.entries)} entries, ids match {same_ids}, "
          f"paths match {same_paths}, flags match {same_flags}")

    verify = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="ds3-fog-verify-"))
    for e in b2.entries:
        name = e.path.replace("\\", "/").rsplit("/", 1)[-1]
        if name in {f["file"] for f in changed_files}:
            (verify / name).write_bytes(e.data)
    vcfg = dict(cfg, dir=str(verify), out=str(verify), dryRun=True,
                report=str(verify / "report.json"), roundtripCheck=False)
    vrep = run_node(vcfg)
    # Compare as MULTISETS, not dicts: several particles in one effect can share
    # an effect id, action type, texture and width, and a dict would silently
    # collapse them and report 35 of 35 where there are 50 to check.
    def key(c, fade):
        return (c["file"], c["action"], c["fogTextures"], round(c["width"] or 0, 3),
                round(fade, 3))
    want = sorted(key(c, c["newFade"]) for c in report["changes"])
    got = sorted(key(c, c["oldFade"]) for c in vrep["changes"])
    on = all(c["oldDepthBlend"] for c in vrep["changes"])
    print(f"  read back from the built binder: {len(got)} particles found, "
          f"{'all ' + str(len(want)) + ' match' if got == want else 'MISMATCH'} the new "
          f"{args.field}; depthBlend on for all: {on}")
    if got != want:
        print(f"    expected {want}\n    got      {got}")

    rel = out.relative_to(HOME)
    print("\nto deploy (NOT done automatically, the harness cannot capture m32 yet):")
    print("  mkdir -p ~/couch/data/ds3-shot/game/mod/sfx")
    print(f"  cp ~/{rel} ~/couch/data/ds3-shot/game/mod/sfx/{out.name}")
    shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)
    shutil.rmtree(verify, ignore_errors=True)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
